 "about_text": "Gallery Tsubaki is a contemporary art gallery in the Kyobashi district of Tokyo, near Ginza. According to the gallery's own diary, its director left his father's gallery, Tsubaki Kindai Garou, to open Gallery Tsubaki around 1984. Since then it has built a program centered on Japanese artists working across painting, sculpture, ceramics, woodblock printmaking and photography, with a particular fondness for surreal, fantastical and meticulously crafted imagery. The gallery represents a large roster of emerging and mid-career Japanese artists, several of whom it has shown continuously for decades, and it regularly places their work in international art fairs across Taipei, Seoul, Busan and beyond, positioning itself as an advocate for Japanese contemporary art in the wider Asian market.",
 "source_kind": "official",
